From: guille-vega <guillermo.vega@balena.io>
Subject: DEBUG: Trace the boot from the SPL to U-Boot proper

Temporary, do not merge. U-Boot proper of the iot-gate-imx8plus runs through
init_sequence_f, asks for a system reset and the board restarts, without any
readable output of its console. Find what asks for it:

- the SPL prints the reset cause of the previous boot (SRC_SRSR) as soon as it
  has a console, and clears it, so each boot shows its own
- the SPL prints where it jumps to and the first words found at U-Boot and at
  the FDT
- U-Boot proper writes a marker to UART2 between the steps of init_sequence_f
  and init_sequence_r and, before it relocates, the values that crt0 uses for
  the new stack and gd, and the state of the console and the version string
- everything that U-Boot proper asks its console to print is also written to
  UART2 directly
- panic() and a system reset write to UART2 their message, and the words of
  the stack that point into U-Boot, as link addresses, to be looked up in the
  symbols that the build prints in the log of do_compile

---

